**Date:** 28 October 2026 · **Replaces:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) once accepted

## Context

Under 0001 the desk merged by subject line. #4471 took 412 reports under subjects such as
"Wrong day on the invite" and was marked *known, one fix queued*. It held three problems
([#4471 split](/kb/incidents/4471-split)); the queued fix closed one of them.

## Decision

Two reports are the same issue when they share a cause (`causes.ts`, tried in
[triage](/kb/triage/dedupe)): the tenant's locale and booking form, the channel, and what the
report says happened. The subject line is a search aid, not a reason to merge.

## Consequences

- Triage reads the body, not just the subject. Slower per report; far fewer tickets marked known
  while part of them is still broken.
- A big ticket gets its cause table read before it is marked *known*.
- 0001 stays as written; this record replaces it once accepted.

